@page "/intermediate/052"

<h1>Exercise 052 - JsInteropModule</h1>

@* Same reasoning as Ex050: the module import happens from OnAfterRenderAsync, which
   Blazor also invokes during the static prerender pass - and there's no live JS
   runtime to import a module against yet at that point. Prerender is disabled on the
   COMPONENT, not the page, so the page (this heading) stays statically delivered;
   only the component's own interactive render is deferred to the circuit. Unlike
   Ex049/Ex050, the JS side here isn't an inline <script> global - it's a real,
   separately-served module file at wwwroot/app.js, dynamically imported by
   IJSRuntime.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./app.js"). *@
<Ex052_JsInteropModule @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
